          %p In order to put our discussion in perspective, we start by surveying some
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "#HistoryAndBackground"} History and background
              \.
          %p
            Then in order to lay the basis of all our discussion to follow, which is super
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Lie+theory"} higher Lie theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebras"} super Lie algebras
            and discuss their generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} super L-∞ algebras
            (whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"} formal duals
            are called “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FDA"}> FDA
            ”s in the physics literature):
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "#SuperLInfinityCohomologyAndFDAs"} Super L-infinity cohomology and FDAs
              \.
          %p
            We will be associating a fundamental
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "-cocycle." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#FromCocyclesToWZW"} From L-infinity-cocycles to higher WZW models
          %p
            The basic example of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebras"} super Lie algebras
            that induces all phenomena to follow are the super-translation parts of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            algebras, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetimes"} super Minkowski spacetimes
            introduced in detail in
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+supersymmetry"} geometry of physics – supersymmetry
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "#SuperMinowskiSpacetimes"} Super Minkowski spacetimes
              \.
          %p
            The key phenomena to be discussed are then the non-trivial invariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            in the super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetimes"} super Minkowski spacetimes
            (sometimes called
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tau+cohomology"} tau cohomology
            in the physics literature). Computationally these correspond to certain identities satisfied by qadrilinear expressions in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Majorana+spinors"} Majorana spinors
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fierz+identities"} Fierz identities
            and so we pause to explain these in
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "#FierzIdentities"} Fierz identities
              \.
          %p
            This then gives rise to the “old
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+super-string"} Green-Schwarz super-string
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-membranes"} super-membranes
            = succeed "-invariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spin
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetimes"} super Minkowski spacetimes
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tau+cohomology"}> tau cohomology
            ):
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "#TheSuperStringAndTheSuperMembrane"} The super-string and the super-membrane
              \.
          %p
            Using our previously established general theory of super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra+cohomology"}> L-∞ algebra cohomology
            , we see that the cocycles in the old
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/brane+scan"} brane scan
            classify
            %em higher
            central extensions of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetimes"} super Minkowski spacetimes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+n-algebras"} super Lie n-algebras
            called
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+super+Minkowski+spacetimes"} extended super Minkowski spacetimes
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#ExtendedSuperMinkowskiSpacetime"} Extended super Minkowski spacetimes
          %p
            A key point then is that these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+n-algebras"} super Lie n-algebras
            obtained from
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
            %em further
            super
            = succeed "-cocycles," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetimes"} super Minkowski spacetimes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            and to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#TheSuperDBranes"} The super D-branes and the M5-brane
          %p
            This gives a tree of consecutive invariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+higher+central+extensions"} universal higher central extensions
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+n-algebras"} super Lie n-algebras
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/brane+bouquet"} brane bouquet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descend
            these iterated central extensions to single but non-central higher cocycles. The result turns out to be the image in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            of the classifying maps of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+fields"} background fields
            in
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            = succeed "-twisted" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-field"} B-field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/RR-fields"} RR-fields
            and the M-flux fields. This we discuss in
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "#Fields"} Fields
              \.
          %p
            There turn out to be special relations among these. In particular passing from super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra+cohomology"} L-∞ algebra cohomology
            to the corresponding
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+cohomology"} cyclic cohomology
            turns out to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
            operation of what in physics is called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"} branes
            (here: of their
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+fields"} background fields
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a{:href => "#DoubleDimensionalReduction"} Double dimensional reduction
              \.
          %p
            By systematically applying this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+n-algebra"} super Lie n-algebraic
            formalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+cohomology"} cyclic cohomology
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dualities+in+string+theory"} dualities in string theory
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rationally
          %ul
            %li
              %em>
                %a{:href => "#Dualities"} Dualities
              \.
          %h2#HistoryAndBackground History and background
          %p
            Below we present fundamental
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-branes"} super p-branes
            as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+exceptionalism"} exceptional
            algebro-geometric structures that are discovered by applying the magnifying glass (namely a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitehead+tower"} Whitehead tower
            construction) of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+n-algebra"} super Lie n-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            to the atom of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspace"} superspace
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FSS13"} FSS 13
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FSS15"} FSS 15
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#FSS16a"} FSS 16a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#FSS16b"} FSS 16b
          %p
            This is not the perspective from which
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-branes"} super p-branes
            were arrived at historically. In order to put our discussion into perspective, here we briefly review some of the historical background.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} Perturbative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            on geometric backgrounds is defined by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond+model"} Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+super+conformal+field+theories"} 2d super conformal field theories
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+charge"} central charge
            15) on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheets"} worldsheets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            that are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Riemann+surfaces"} super Riemann surfaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spaces"} target spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            that are ordinary (i.e. “bosonic”)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
          %p
            These
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theories"} field theories
            are induced from
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functionals"} action functionals
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy+functional"} energy functional
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polyakov+action"}> Polyakov action
            ) on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma,X]
            of smooth functions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi \;\colon\; \Sigma \longrightarrow X
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            to target
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            The central theorem of perturbative superstring theory (the no ghost theorem with
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GSO+projection"} GSO projection
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
            are the quanta of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbation+theory"} perturbations
            of a higher dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+theory"} field theory
            on target spacetime, hence transforms under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            on target spacetime.
          %p This is the fundamental prediction of the assumption of fundamental strings:
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                assuming that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+particles"} fundamental particles
                that run in
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Feynman+diagrams"} Feynman diagrams
                are fundamentally (at high energy) the ground state modes of a fundamental
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string"} string
            %li
              %p
                demanding that there are
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermionic
                particles among these,
          %p implies
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                that the string must be the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+string"} spinning string
                (have fermions in its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
                theory), which in turn implies…
            %li
              %p
                that it is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
                (worldsheet
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
                mixes the worldsheet bosons and fermions), precisely: the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond+superstring"} Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond superstring
            %li
              %p
                that its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
                theory, hence that also the effective target space fields exhibit
                %em local
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
                (i.e. “high energy supersymmetry”, different from “low energy supersymmetry” that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LHC"} LHC
                was looking for).
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  main theorem of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+string+theory"} perturbative super-string theory
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %munder
                            %mrow
                              %mtext fermions
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mo +
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mtext strings
                            %mo ⏟
                          %mtext spinning string
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtext superstring
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⇒
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtext supergravity
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\text{spinning string}}{\underbrace{\text{fermions} \;+\; \text{strings}}} \;=\; \text{superstring} \;\Rightarrow\; \text{supergravity}
          %p
            The first step in this implication (identifying the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spinning+string"} spinning string
            as the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            was discovered in “the west”, in the first place), but the second step (that the superstring excitations necessarily are quanta of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            theory) appears as a miracle from the point of view of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond+superstring"} Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond superstring
          %p
            In order to improve on this situation,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"} Michael Green
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} John Schwarz
            searched for and found (
            %a{:href => "#GreenSchwarz81"}> Green-Schwarz 81
            ,
            %a{:href => "#GreenSchwarz82"} Green-Schwarz 82
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#GreenSchwarz84"} Green-Schwarz 84
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Schwarz16"} Schwarz 16, slides 24-25
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            that would manifestly exhibit
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
                  for
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
                %th
                  manifest
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz+super-string"} Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz super-string
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Green-Schwarz super-string
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  on
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
          %p
            The basic idea is to pass to the evident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometric
            analogue of the bosonic string action:
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed manifold
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            2 – representing the abstract
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            of a string. Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+manifold"} pseudo-Riemannian manifold
            – representing a purely
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravity"} gravitational
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            background. Then the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            governing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string"} bosonic string
            propagating in this spacetime is the functional
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mi ℏ
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi bos
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℝ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi ℏ
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar} S_{bos})
                  \\;\colon\;
                  [\Sigma,X]
                  \\longrightarrow
                  \\mathbb{R}/_{\hbar}\mathbb{Z}
          %p
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma,X]
            (of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma \to X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relativity"} relativistic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume"} volume
            of the image of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldsheet"} worldsheet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ϕ
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ↦
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi kin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %msub
                    %mi vol
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo *
                      %mi g
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Sigma\overset{\phi}{\longrightarrow} X)
                  \\;\mapsto\;
                  S_{kin}(\phi)
                  \\coloneqq
                  \\int_\Sigma vol_{\phi^\ast g}
                  \\,.
          %p
            (This is the
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nambu-Goto+action"} Nambu-Goto action
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Polyakov+action"} Polyakov action
            which is the genuine starting point for the quantum
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz+super-string"} Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz super-string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/p-branes"} p-branes
            it is more natural to consider the Nambu-Goto form of the action here.)
          %p
            When here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
            is generalized to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superspacetime"} superspacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+structure"} orthogonal structure
            encoded by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-vielbein"} super-vielbein
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergeometry"} supergeometric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma,X]
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superisometry+group"} superisometry group
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,g)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mtext symmetry of worldsheet theory
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mtable
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %mi Σ
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %msup
                                    %mrow
                                    %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                      %mi ϕ
                                  %mo ↙
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %msup
                                    %mo ↘
                                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi ϕ
                                        %mo ′
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mi X
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %munder
                                    %mo ⟶
                                    %mo ≃
                                %mtd
                                %mtd
                                  %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mtext super-isometry of target spacetime
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\text{symmetry of worldsheet theory}
                  \\\
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \Sigma
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\phi}}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{\phi'}}
                  \\\
                  X &amp;&amp;\underset{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}&amp;&amp; X
                  }
                  \\\
                  \\text{super-isometry of target spacetime}
                  }
          %p
            However,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Green"} Green
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Schwarz"} Schwarz
            noticed that this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kinetic+action"} kinetic action
            functional
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %msub
                    %mi vol
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mo *
                      %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \mapsto \int_\Sigma vol_{\phi^\ast e}
            does
            %em not
            quite yield dynamics that is equivalent to that of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond+super-string"} Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond super-string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equations+of+motion"} equations of motion
            hold (“on
            = succeed "\u201D)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/shell"} shell
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz+super-string"} Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz super-string
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi WZW
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{WZW}
            (whose notation we explain in a moment) to the plain super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nambu-Goto+action"} Nambu-Goto action
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi kin
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{kin}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            enjoys a further 1-parameter
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetry"} symmetry
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kappa-symmetry"} kappa-symmetry
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi GS
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi kin
                  %mo +
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi WZW
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S_{GS} = S_{kin} + S_{WZW}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Moreover, they showed that restricting the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dynamics"} dynamics
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+superstring"} Green-Schwarz superstring
            to the
            = succeed "-symmetric" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi κ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz+super-string"} Neveu-Ramond-Schwarz super-string
          %p
            Finally they showed that when
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fixing"} gauge fixing
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light-cone+gauge"} light-cone gauge
            (which is possible whenever
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target spacetime
            admits two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lightlike"} lightlike
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+vector"} Killing vector
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+string"} Green-Schwarz string
            may be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantized
            by a standard procedure and the resulting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+system"} quantum
            dynamics is equivalent to that of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond+super-string"} Neveu-Schwarz-Ramond super-string
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof"} proof
            for the observed local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+spacetime"} target spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            of super-string
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+field+theory"} effective field theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+superstring"} Green-Schwarz superstring
            away from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light+cone+gauge"} light cone gauge
            remains an open problem.)
          %p
            While Green-Schwarz’s extra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kappa-symmetry"} kappa-symmetry
            term
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi WZW
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_{WZW}
            this serves a clear purpose as a means to an end, originally its geometric meaning was mysterious. However, in (
            %a{:href => "#HenneauxMezincescu85"}> Henneaux-Mezincescu 85
            ) it was observed (expanded on in (
            %a{:href => "#Rabin87"}> Rabin 87
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AzcarragaTownsend89"} Azcarraga-Townsend 89
            = succeed "))," do
              %a{:href => "#AzcarragaIzquierdo95"} Azcarraga-Izquierdo 95,chapter 8
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            describing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-string"} super-string
            in
            = succeed "-dimensions" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d+1
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parameterized+WZW+model"} parameterized
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wess-Zumino-Witten+model"} Wess-Zumino-Witten model
            for
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
                being locally
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi d
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{d-1,1|\mathbf{N}}
                regarded as the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coset"} coset
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"} supergroup
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
