                  \\;+\;
                  (C \Gamma^{a_1 \cdots a_p})_{\alpha \beta} Z_{a_1, \cdots, a_p}
          %p
            (for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+spinor"} Killing spinor
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            its corresponding
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+vector"} Killing vector
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/type+II+supersymmetry+algebra"} type II supersymmetry algebra
            and the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory+supersymmetry+algebra"} M-theory supersymmetry algebra
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AGIT89"} Azcárraga-Gauntlett-Izquierdo-Townsend 89
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity+algebra+extensions"} Lie n-algebra extensions
            of which the familiar super Lie algebra extensions are the 0-truncation (
            %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiber15"}> Sati-Schreiber 15
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Local+prequantum+field+theory"} Khavkine-Schreiber 16
          %p
            In summary, the nature and classification of Green-Schwarz action functionals captures in a mathematically precise way a good deal of the core structure of
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
          %p
            In fact, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-infinity+algebra"} super Lie-n algebraic
            perspective on the Green-Schwarz functionals via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/brane+bouquet"} brane bouquet
            also solves the following open problem on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-branes"} M-branes
          %p
            it is famously known from
            = succeed "-cancellation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freed-Witten+anomaly"} Freed-Witten anomaly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane+charges"} D-brane charges
            are not in fact just in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+cohomology"} de Rham cohomology
            in every second degree, but are in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rationally
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+de+Rham+cohomology"} twisted de Rham cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F1-brane"} F1-brane
            charge (from the fundamental). It is an open problem to determine what becomes of these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
            charge groups as one lifts F1/D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            \-branes in string theory to M2/M5-branes in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                %th intersecting branes
                %th
                  charges in
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F1-brane"}> F1
                  \/
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-brane"} Dp-branes
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+K-theory"} twisted K-theory
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M2-brane"}> M2
                  \/
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} ???
          %p
            Notice that there are “microscopic degrees of freedom” of the theory encoded by the choice of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            here, generalizing the extra degrees of freedom in the choice of a WZW-term already mentioned above. In general for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            a cohomology theory and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \longrightarrow E \otimes \mathbb{Q}
            its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+character"} Chern character
            map (for instance from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            in every second degree), then a choice of genuine charges is the extra information encoded in a lift
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mtext true charge
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mi ch
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mtext rational
                              %mrow
                                %mtext charge
                        %mtd
                          %mi E
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; E
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\text{true charge}}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{ch}}
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\underset{\text{rational} \atop  \text{charge}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; E \otimes \mathbb{Q}
                  }
          %p
            But
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rationally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/The+brane+bouquet"} The brane bouquet
            allows to derive this from first principles:
          %p
            Above we saw that the naive cocycles of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            and of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            are not defined on the actual
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+super+infinity-groupoid"} smooth super infinity-groupoid
            extension of spacetime. Hence we should ask if these cocycles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descend
            to the actual super-spacetime while picking up some twists.
          %p One may prove that:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the F1/D
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                \-brane GS-WZW cocycles descend to 10d type II superspacetime to form a single cocycle in rational twisted K-theory, just as the traditional lore reqires (
                %a{:href => "#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber16"}> Fiorenza-Sati-Schreiber 16
                );
            %li
              %p
                the M2/M5 GS-WZW cocycles descent to 11d superspacetime to form a single cocycle with values in the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+n-sphere"} rational 4-sphere
                (
                %a{:href => "#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber16"}> Fiorenza-Sati-Schreiber 16
                ).
          %p
            This has implications on some open conjectures regarding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M-theory"} M-theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Equivariant+cohomology+of+M2%2FM5-branes"} Equivariant cohomology of M2/M5-branes
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p We now explain all this in detail.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h2#SuperLInfinityCohomologyAndFDAs
            Super
            = succeed "-cohomology" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %p
            We recall
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebras"} super Lie algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
            description in terms of their
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebras"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} super L-∞ algebras
            are, again they are conveniently expressed (if they are of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+dual"} formal dual
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebras"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebras
          #SuperLieAlgebraAsLieAlgebraInternalToSuperVectorSpaces.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sVect
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Vect
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi τ
                      %mi super
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sVect = (Vect^{\mathbb{Z}/2}, \otimes_k, \tau^{super} )
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+space"} super vector space
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔤
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              %li
                %p a homomorphism
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi k
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        [-,-] \;\colon\; \mathfrak{g} \otimes_k \mathfrak{g} \longrightarrow \mathfrak{g}
                %p
                  of super vector spaces (the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em super Lie bracket
            %p such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the bracket is skew-symmetric in that the following
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagram commutes
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi 𝔤
                                %msub
                                  %mo ⊗
                                  %mi k
                                %mi 𝔤
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %msubsup
                                      %mi τ
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi 𝔤
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mi 𝔤
                                      %mi super
                              %mtd
                                %mi 𝔤
                                %msub
                                  %mo ⊗
                                  %mi k
                                %mi 𝔤
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                      %mo ,
                                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                      %mo ,
                                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi 𝔤
                              %mtd
                                %munder
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mn 1
                              %mtd
                                %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \\mathfrak{g} \otimes_k \mathfrak{g}
                        \&amp;
                        \\overset{\tau^{super}_{\mathfrak{g},\mathfrak{g}}}{\longrightarrow}
                        \&amp;
                        \\mathfrak{g} \otimes_k \mathfrak{g}
                        \\\
                        {}^{\mathllap{[-,-]}}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^{\mathrlap{[-,-]}}
                        \\\
                        \\mathfrak{g} &amp;\underset{-1}{\longrightarrow}&amp; \mathfrak{g}
                        }
                %p
                  (here
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi τ
                          %mi super
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tau^{super}
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
                  in the category of
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
                  holds in that the following
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} diagram commutes
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mi 𝔤
                                %msub
                                  %mo ⊗
                                  %mi k
                                %mi 𝔤
                                %msub
                                  %mo ⊗
                                  %mi k
                                %mi 𝔤
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mover
                                  %mo ⟶
                                  %mrow
                                    %msubsup
                                      %mi τ
                                      %mrow
                                        %mi 𝔤
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mi 𝔤
                                      %mi super
                                    %msub
                                      %mo ⊗
                                      %mi k
                                    %mi id
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi 𝔤
                                %msub
                                  %mo ⊗
                                  %mi k
                                %mi 𝔤
                                %msub
                                  %mo ⊗
                                  %mi k
                                %mi 𝔤
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                      %mrow
                                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                        %mo ,
                                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                    %mo −
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                %mo ↘
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mo ↙
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                      %mo ,
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                      %mo ,
                                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mi 𝔤
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \\mathfrak{g} \otimes_k \mathfrak{g} \otimes_k \mathfrak{g}
                        \&amp;&amp;
                        \\overset{\tau^{super}_{\mathfrak{g}, \mathfrak{g}} \otimes_k id }{\longrightarrow}
                        \&amp;&amp;
                        \\mathfrak{g} \otimes_k \mathfrak{g} \otimes_k \mathfrak{g}
                        \\\
                        \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{[-,[-,-]]} - [[-,-],-] }\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{[-,[-,-]]}}
                        \\\
                        \&amp;&amp; \mathfrak{g}
                        }
                        \\,.
          %p Externally this means the following:
          #SuperLieAlgebraTraditional.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
              according to def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperLieAlgebraAsLieAlgebraInternalToSuperVectorSpaces"}
              is equivalently
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mi even
                          %mo ⊕
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mi odd
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_{even} \oplus \mathfrak{g}_{odd}
              %li
                %p
                  equipped with a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+map"} bilinear map
                  (the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %em super Lie bracket
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %msub
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi k
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo →
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        [-,-] : \mathfrak{g}\otimes_k \mathfrak{g} \to \mathfrak{g}
                %p
                  which is
                  %em graded
                  skew-symmetric: for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y \in \mathfrak{g}
                  two elements of homogeneous degree
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi σ
                            %mi x
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_x
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi σ
                            %mi y
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_y
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mi x
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        [x,y] = -(-1)^{\sigma_x \sigma_y} [y,x]
                        \\,,
              %li
                %p
                  that satisfies the
                  = succeed "-graded" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
                  in that for any three elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x,y,z \in \mathfrak{g}
                  of homogeneous super-degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi σ
                          %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi σ
                          %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi σ
                          %mi z
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_x,\sigma_y,\sigma_z\in \mathbb{Z}_2
                  then
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mi x
                            %mo ⋅
                            %msub
                              %mi σ
                              %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi y
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi x
                        %mo ,
                        %mi z
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        [x, [y, z]] = [[x,y],z] + (-1)^{\sigma_x \cdot \sigma_y} [y, [x,z]]
                        \\,.
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of super Lie algebras is a homomorphisms of the underlying
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
              which preserves the Lie bracket. We write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sLieAlg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    sLieAlg
            %p
              for the resulting
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of super Lie algebras.
          #CEAlgebraofSuperLieAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g})
              is the super-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+vector+space"} dual
              super vector space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\wedge^\bullet  \mathfrak{g}^\ast
            %p
              equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{\mathfrak{g}}
              that on generators is the linear dual of the super Lie bracket
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{\mathfrak{g}} \;\coloneqq\; [-,-]^\ast \;\colon\; \mathfrak{g}^\ast \to \mathfrak{g}^\ast \wedge \mathfrak{g}^\ast
            %p
              and which is extended to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet \mathfrak{g}^\ast
              by the graded Leibniz rule (i.e. as a graded
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p
              Here all elements are
              = succeed "-bigraded," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z} \times \mathbb{Z}/2)
              %em cohomological grading
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} n
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\n \mathfrak{g}^\ast
              %em super-grading
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              (even/odd).
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_i \in CE(\mathfrak{g})
              two elements of homogeneous bi-degree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi σ
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n_i, \sigma_i)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signs+in+supergeometry"} sign rule
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi σ
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mi σ
                          %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi α
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\alpha_1 \wedge \alpha_2 = (-1)^{n_1 n_2} (-1)^{\sigma_1 \sigma_2}\; \alpha_2 \wedge \alpha_1
                    \\,.
            %p
              (See at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signs+in+supergeometry"} signs in supergeometry
              for discussion of this sign rule and of an alternative sign rule that is also in use. )
          %p
            We may think of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g})
            equivalently as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+differential+form"} left-invariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+differential+forms"} super differential forms
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+theory"} corresponding
            simply connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+group"} super Lie group
            \.
          %p
            The concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebras"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebras
            is traditionally introduced as a means to define
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
          #SuperLieAlgebraCohomology.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  an
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                    \-cocycle
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                  (with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
                  in
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℝ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi even
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,even)
                  in its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi CE
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g})
                  (def.
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CEAlgebraofSuperLieAlgebra"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi 𝕘
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{\mathbb{g}}
                  closed.
              %li
                %p
                  the cocycle is non-trivial if it is not
                  = succeed "-exact" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi d
                            %mi 𝔤
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{\mathfrak{g}}
              %li
                %p
                  hene the
                  %em
                    super-
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra cohomology
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                  (with
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
                  in
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℝ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
                  of its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi H
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi H
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi CE
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        H^\bullet(\mathfrak{g}, \mathbb{R}) = H^\bullet(CE(\mathfrak{g}))
                        \\,.
          %p
            The following says that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            is an equivalent incarnation of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
          #FormalDualCE.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p The functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi sLieAlg
                      %mi fin
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi dgAlg
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CE \;\colon\; sLieAlg^{fin}  \hookrightarrow dgAlg^{op}
            %p
              that sends a finite dimensional
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              to its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g})
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CEAlgebraofSuperLieAlgebra"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful functor
              which hence exibits
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebras"} super Lie algebras
              as a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential-graded+algebras"} differential-graded algebras
          %p
            This makes it immediate how to generalize to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-infinity+algebras"} super L-infinity algebras
          #SuperLInfinityAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} super L-∞ algebra
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal to
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "geometry+of+physics+--+superalgebra#CategoryOfSuperVectorSpaces"}> def.
              ).
          %p Explicitly this means the following:
          #SuperGradedSignatureOfPermutation.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              %strong (super graded signature of a permutation)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              be a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+object"} graded
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+space"} super vector space
              = succeed "-bigraded" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \times (\mathbb{Z}/2)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              let
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi v
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{v} = (v_1, v_2, \cdots, v_n)
            %p
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-tuple"} n-tuple
              of elements of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              of homogeneous degree
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi n
                        %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n_i, s_i) \in \mathbb{Z} \times \mathbb{Z}/2
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %msub
                        %mi V
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi n
                            %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi s
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i \in V_{(n_i,s_i)}
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permutation
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              elements, write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)^{\vert \sigma \vert}
              for the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+of+a+permutation"} signature of the permutation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)^k
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
              is the composite of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              permutations that each exchange precisely one pair of neighboring elements.
            %p
              We say that the
              %em
                super
                = succeed "-graded" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi v
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{v}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi χ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi σ
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\chi(\sigma, v_1, \cdots, v_n) \;\in\; \{-1,+1\}
            %p
              is the product of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signature+of+a+permutation"} signature of the permutation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi σ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)^{\vert \sigma \vert}
              with a factor of
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi n
                          %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi i
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (-1)^{n_i n_j}(-1)^{s_i s_j}
            %p
              for each interchange of neighbours
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\cdots v_i,v_j, \cdots )
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi j
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\cdots v_j,v_i, \cdots )
              involved in the decomposition of the permuation as a sequence of swapping neighbour pairs (see at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/signs+in+supergeometry"} signs in supergeometry
              for discussion of this combination of super-grading and homological grading).
          %p
            Now def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperLInfinityAlgebra"}
            is equivalent to the following def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#sLInfinityDefinitionViaGeneralizedJacobiIdentity"}
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#L-infinity-algebra#DefinitionViaHigherBrackets"} L-infinity algebras
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi χ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
            now given by def.
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperGradedSignatureOfPermutation"}
          #sLInfinityDefinitionViaGeneralizedJacobiIdentity.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              An
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} super L-∞ algebra
              is
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo ×
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℤ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z} \times (\mathbb{Z}/2)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+object"} graded
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔤
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multilinear+map"} multilinear map
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                      \-ary bracket
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi l
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ≔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %munder
                          %munder
                            %mrow
                              %mi 𝔤
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi ⋯
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mi 𝔤
                            %mo ⏟
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mtext copies
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        l_n(\cdots)
                        \\;\coloneqq\;
                        [-,-, \cdots, -]_n
                        \\;\colon\;
                        \\underset{n \; \text{copies}}{\underbrace{\mathfrak{g} \otimes \cdots \otimes \mathfrak{g}}}
                        \\longrightarrow
                        \\mathfrak{g}
                %p
                  and of degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-2
            %p such that the following conditions hold:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  (
                  %strong> super graded skew symmetry
                  ) each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi l
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} l_n
                  is graded antisymmetric, in that for every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permutation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  elements and for every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-tuple"} n-tuple
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (v_1, \cdots, v_n)
                  of homogeneously graded elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i \in \mathfrak{g}_{\vert v_i \vert}
                  then
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi l
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi χ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi σ
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⋅
                        %msub
                          %mi l
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        l_n(v_{\sigma(1)}, v_{\sigma(2)},\cdots ,v_{\sigma(n)})
                        \=
                        \\chi(\sigma,v_1,\cdots, v_n) \cdot l_n(v_1, v_2, \cdots v_n)
                %p
                  where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi χ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi σ
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi(\sigma,v_1,\cdots, v_n)
                  is the super
                  = succeed "-graded" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (v_1,\cdots,v_n)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi σ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperGradedSignatureOfPermutation"}
              %li
                %p
                  (
                  %strong>
                    strong homotopy
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobi+identity"} Jacobi identity
                  ) for all
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi ℕ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-tuple"} (n+1)-tuples
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (v_1, \cdots, v_{n+1})
                  of homogeneously graded elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i \in \mathfrak{g}_{\vert v_i \vert}
                  the followig
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equation"} equation
                  holds
                #eq:LInfinityJacobiIdentity.maruku-equation
                  %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo ,
                                %mi j
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi ℕ
                            %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo +
                                %mi j
                                %mo =
                                %mi n
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                        %munder
                          %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                          %mrow
                            %mi σ
                            %mo ∈
                            %mi UnShuff
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi χ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi σ
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi j
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %msub
                          %mi l
                          %mi j
                        %mrow
                          %mo (
                          %msub
                            %mi l
                            %mi i
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mrow
                                %mi σ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ⋯
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi v
                              %mrow
                                %mi σ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi i
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo )
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mrow
                              %mi σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi i
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ,
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi v
                            %mrow
                              %mi σ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi n
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\sum_{{i,j \in \mathbb{N}} \atop {i+j = n+1}}
                        \\sum_{\sigma \in UnShuff(i,j)}
                        \\chi(\sigma,v_1, \cdots, v_{n})
                        (-1)^{i(j-1)}
                        l_{j} \left(
                        l_i \left( v_{\sigma(1)}, \cdots, v_{\sigma(i)} \right),
                        v_{\sigma(i+1)} , \cdots , v_{\sigma(n)}
                        \\right)
                        \= 0
                        \\,,
                %p
                  where the inner sum runs over all
                  = succeed "-" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi i
                          %mo ,
                          %mi j
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i,j)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unshuffles"} unshuffles
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma
                  and where
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi χ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \chi
                  is the super graded signature sign from def.
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperGradedSignatureOfPermutation"}
            %p
              A
              %em
                strict
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of super
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi is
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    is
                    
                    \\mathfrak{g}_1 \longrightarrow \mathfrak{g}_2
            %p
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
              that preserves the bidegree and all the brackets, in an evident sens.
            %p
              A
              %em strong homotopy homomorphism
              (“sh map”) of super
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+duals"} formal duals
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperLInfinityCEAlgebra"}
          #LInfinityTerminology.num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              Special cases of the general concept of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} super L-∞ algebras
              def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#sLInfinityDefinitionViaGeneralizedJacobiIdentity"}
              go by special names:
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} super L-∞ algebra
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              is concentrated in even
              = succeed "-degree," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
            %p
              If the only possibly non-vanishing brackets of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              are the unary one
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-]
              (which induces the structure of a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              on
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
