          #SuperLInfintiyAsFDA.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (history of the concept of (super-)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                algebras)
            %p
              The identification of the concept of (super-)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              \-algebras has a non-linear history:
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
              in the incarnation of higher brackets satisfying a higher Jacobi identity,
            %p
              def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#sLInfinityDefinitionViaGeneralizedJacobiIdentity"}
              and remark
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LInfinityTerminology"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/L-infinity-algebra#LadaStasheff92"} Lada-Stasheff 92
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BRST+complex"} BRST complex
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bosonic+string"} bosonic string
              that was found in the construction of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+string+field+theory"} closed string field theory
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "string+field+theory#Zwiebach93"} Zwiebach 92
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#L-infinity-algebra#Stasheff16"} Stasheff 16
            %p
              The observation that these systems of higher brackets are fully characterized by their Chevalley-Eilenberg dg-(co-)algebras (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SuperLInfinityCEAlgebra"}
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/L-infinity-algebra#LadaMarkl94"} Lada-Markl 94
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiberStasheff08"} Sati-Schreiber-Stasheff 08, around def. 13
            %p
              But in this dual incarnation,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
              and more generally
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} super L-∞ algebras
              (of
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
              literature already in
              %a{:href => "#DAuriaFreRegge80"} D’Auria-Fré-Regge 80
              and explicitly in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Nieuwenhuizen82"} van Nieuwenhuizen 82
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%27Auria-Fr%C3%A9+formulation+of+supergravity"} D'Auria-Fré formulation of supergravity
              (
              %a{:href => "#DAuriaFre82"}> D’Auria-Fré 82
              ) and eventually came to be referred to as “FDA”s (short for “free differential algebra”) in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
              literature (but beware that these dg-algebras are in general
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+construction"} free
              only as graded-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supercommutative+superalgebras"}> supercommutative superalgebras
              , not as differential algebras) The relation between super
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
              literature is made explicit in (
              %a{:href => "#FSS13"}> FSS 13
              ).
            %table
              %thead
                %tr
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Lie+theory"} higher Lie theory
                  %th
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
              %tbody
                %tr
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+n-algebra"} super Lie n-algebra
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔤
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                  %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
                    “FDA”
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi CE
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g})
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p
              The construction in
              %a{:href => "#Nieuwenhuizen82"} van Nieuwenhuizen 82
              in turn was motivated by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+algebras"} Sullivan algebras
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
              (
              %a{:href => "#rational+homotopy+theory#Sullivan77"}> Sullivan 77
              ). Indeed, their dual incarnations in rational homotopy theory are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebras"} dg-Lie algebras
              (
              %a{:href => "#rational+homotopy+theory#Quillen69"}> Quillen 69
              ), hence a special case of
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LInfinityTerminology"}
            %p
              This close relation between
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+Lie+theory"} higher Lie theory
              might have remained less of a secret had it not been for the focus of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+minimal+models"} Sullivan minimal models
              on the non-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
              case, which excludes the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebras"} Lie algebras
              from the picture. But the Quillen model of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
              effectively says that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+topological+space"} rational topological space
              then its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space"} loop space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega X
              is reflected, infinitesimally, by an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+construction"} Sullivan construction
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
              was concretely identified as higher
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Lie+integration#Henriques"} Henriques 08
              = succeed "-theoretic" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
              manifest is in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "rational+homotopy+theory#BuijsFelixMurillo12"} Buijs-Félix-Murillo 12, section 2
          %p
            However, what has not been used in the “FDA” literature is that super
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            = succeed ":" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/model+structure+for+L-infinity+algebras#Pridham"}> Pridham 10, prop. 4.36
                )
            %p
              There exists a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+objects"} fibrant objects
                  are the (super-)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
                %p
                  with the above
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
                  between them;
              %li
                %p and
                %ul
                  %li
                    %p
                      the weak equivalences between (super-)
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                      \-algebras are the
                      = succeed ";" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
                  %li
                    %p
                      fibrations between (super-)
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi L
                              %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                      \-algebras are the surjections
                %p
                  on the underlying
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
                  (using the unary part of the differential).
            %p
              For more see at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+L-infinity+algebras"} model structure for L-infinity algebras
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            Concretely, this implies in particular that every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} super L-∞ algebras
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi f
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathfrak{g}_1
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{f}}\searrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathfrak{g}_2
                  }
          %p
            is the composite of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
            followed by a surjection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mtext quasi-iso
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mover
                              %mi 𝔤
                              %mo ˜
                            %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mi f
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mo ↙
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %msub
                                      %mi f
                                      %mi fib
                                %mrow
                                  %mtext surjection
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mn 2
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathfrak{g}_1
                  \&amp;&amp; \overset{\text{quasi-iso}}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp;
                  \\widetilde \mathfrak{g}_1
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{f}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow_{\mathrlap{ {f_{fib}} \atop {\text{surjection}}}}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathfrak{g}_2
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            That surjective homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi f
                    %mi fib
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_{fib}
          %p
            is called a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrant+replacement"} fibrant replacement
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_8 Definition
            %p
              Given
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} super L-∞ algebras
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mi f
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathfrak{g}_1 \overset{f}{\longrightarrow} \mathfrak{g}_2
            %p
              then its
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hofib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hofib(f)
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
              of any fibrant replacement
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hofib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi fib
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    hofib(f)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    ker(f_{fib})
                    \\,.
          %p
            Standard facts in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            assert that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hofib
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hofib(f)
            is well-defined up to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Introduction+to+Stable+homotopy+theory+--+P#HomotopyFibers"} Introduction to homotopy theory – Homotopy fibers
          %p
            The following is the key fact about homotopy fibers in the homotopy theory of super
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          #HomotopyFibersOfLInfinityCocycles.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a{:href => "#FSS13"}> Fiorenza-Sati-Schreiber 13, theorem 3.5
                )
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    b^{p+1}\mathbb{R}
            %p
              for the
              = succeed "," do
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+Lie+n-algebra"} line Lie (p+1)-algebra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mo ∧
                        %mo •
                      %munder
                        %munder
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %msub
                              %mi c
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo +
                                %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo ⏟
                        %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mtext single generator
                          %mrow
                            %mtext in deg.
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi p
                            %mo +
                            %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %mi even
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi B
                            %mrow
                              %mi p
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mi ℝ
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CE(b^{p+1}\mathbb{R})
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left(
                    \\wedge^\bullet \underset{\text{single generator} \atop \text{in deg.} \, (p+2,even)}{\underbrace{\langle c_{p+2} \rangle}}
                    \\;,\;
                    d_{B^{p+1}\mathbb{R}} = 0
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              A
              = succeed "-cocycle" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p+2)
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mu_{p+2} \;\colon\; \mathfrak{g} \longrightarrow B^{p+1}\mathbb{R}
                    \\,.
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber"} homotopy fiber
              of this map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi 𝔤
                              %mo ^
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi hofib
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msub
                                    %mi μ
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi p
                                      %mo +
                                      %mn 2
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi 𝔤
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo ⟶
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi μ
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi p
                                    %mo +
                                    %mn 2
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi B
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                            %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\widehat{\mathfrak{g}}
                    \\\
                    {}^{\mathllap{hofib(\mu_{p+2})}}\downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\mathfrak{g}
                    \&amp;\underset{\mu_{p+2}}{\longrightarrow}&amp; B^{p+1}\mathbb{R}
                    }
            %p
              is given by adjoining to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g})
              a single generator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b_{p+1}
            %p
              forced to be a potential for
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi μ
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo +
                          %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_{p+2}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi b
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CE(\widehat{\mathfrak{g}})
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    CE(\mathfrak{g})[b_{p+1}]/(d b_{p+1} = \mu_{p+2})
                    \\,.
          %p
            As a slogan:
            %em
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+central+extensions"} higher central extensions
              classified by higher cocycles are their
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fibers"} homotopy fibers
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              The homotopy fiber of a 2-cocycle on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
              is the classical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extension"} central extension
              that it classifies:
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              be a super Lie algebra of finite dimension, and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mn 2
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_2 \in \wedge^2 \mathfrak{g}^\ast
              be a 2-cocycle
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi 𝔤
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mn 2
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{\mathfrak{g}} \omega_2 = 0
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyFibersOfLInfinityCocycles"}
              says that the homotopy fiber
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{\mathfrak{g}} \longrightarrow \mathfrak{g}
              of the corresponding morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ω
                          %mn 2
                    %mi b
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g} \overset{\omega_2}{\longrightarrow} b \mathbb{R}
              has
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              that of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              with one new generator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in \wedge^1 (\widehat {\mathfrak{g}})
              adjoined, with differential given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %mi c
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{\mathfrak{g}} c = \omega_2
                    \\,.
            %p
              Now by def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CEAlgebraofSuperLieAlgebra"}
              this differential enocodes the linear dual of the Lie bracket. Hence if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              denotes the dual element of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              then the Lie brakcet of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{\mathfrak{g}}
              is modified on elements of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              to be
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mover
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo ^
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [x,y]_{\widehat{\mathfrak{g}}} = [x,y]_{\mathfrak{g}}+ \omega_2(x,y) k
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is exactly the ordinary formula for the central extension of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ω
                        %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_2
          %h2#FromCocyclesToWZW
            From
            = succeed "-Cocycles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %p
            We have discussed super
            = succeed "-cohomology" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a{:href => "#SuperLInfinityCohomologyAndFDAs"} above
            in generality. Further
            %a{:href => "#Branes"} below
            we consider the exceptional invariant super
            = succeed "-cohomology" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superpoint"} superpoint
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+p-branes"} super p-branes
            as discussed in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            literature. Here, in order to substantiate this, we discuss in generality how by the mathematics of higher
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            every super
            = succeed "-cocycle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
            that may be regarded as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            defining a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            description for a fundamental
            = succeed "-brane." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wess-Zumino-Witten+model"} Wess-Zumino-Witten model
          %h3#HigherLieIntegration Higher Lie integration
          %p
            We discuss differential refinements of the “path method” of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
            for
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-infinity-algebras"} L-infinity-algebras
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DefinitionOfLInfinityFormsOnSimplices"}
            is this:
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_3 Remark
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %em flat
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra+valued+differential+forms"} L-∞ algebra valued differential forms
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  are equivalently the dg-algebra homomorphisms
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi flat
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi Hom
                          %mi dgAlg
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi CE
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ,
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} dR
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\Omega_{flat}(U,\mathfrak{g})
                        \=
                        Hom_{dgAlg}(CE(\mathfrak{g}), \Omega^\bullet(U)_{\mathrm{dR}})
              %li
                %p
                  a finite
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
                  between two such forms is equivalently a homotopy
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi Ω
                                  %mi flat
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi U
                                %mo ×
                                %msup
                                  %mi Δ
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo ,
                                %mi 𝔤
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mrow
                                  %mrow
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %msub
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                      %mn 0
                                %mo ↙
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msup
                                  %mo ↘
                                  %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                    %mrow
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                      %msub
                                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                                        %mn 1
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi Ω
                                  %mi flat
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi U
                                %mo ,
                                %mi 𝔤
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mi Ω
                                  %mi flat
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi U
                                %mo ,
                                %mi 𝔤
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \&amp; &amp; \Omega_{flat}(U \times \Delta^1,\mathfrak{g})
                        \\\
                        \&amp; {}^{(-)|_0}\swarrow &amp;&amp; \searrow^{\mathrlap{(-)|_1}}
                        \\\
                        \\Omega_{flat}(U ,\mathfrak{g})
                        \&amp;&amp; &amp;&amp;
                        \\Omega_{flat}(U, \mathfrak{g})
                        }
                        \\,.
            %p
              For more details see at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/infinity-Lie+algebroid-valued+differential+form#InfGaugeTrafo"} infinity-Lie algebroid-valued differential form – Integration of infinitesimal gauge transformations
          #DefinitionOfLInfinityFormsOnSimplices.num_defn
            %h6#definition_9 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              an
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi CE
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g})
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
                  of an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝔤
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi smth
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo →
                        %mi SmoothMfd
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^\bullet_{smth} \colon \Delta \to SmoothMfd
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosimplicial+object"} cosimplicial
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold+with+corners"} with corners
                  which is in degree
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  the standard
                  = succeed "-simplex" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi k
                          %mo ↪
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %mi k
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^k \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{k+1}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi si
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi smth
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet_{si}(\Delta_{smth}^k)
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
                  of those
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+forms"} differential forms
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi smth
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta_{smth}^k
                  which have
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sitting+instants"} sitting instants
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
                  of the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
                  they are constant perpendicular to any face on their value at that face;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mi si
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ×
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi smth
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet_{si}(U \times \Delta_{smth}^k)
                  for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi SmoothMfd
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in SmoothMfd
                  for the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
                  of differential forms on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ×
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \times \Delta^k
                  which when restricted to each point of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  have sitting instants on
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi k
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^k
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mrow
                            %mi vert
                            %mo ,
                            %mi si
                          %mo •
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ×
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi smth
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet_{vert,si}(U \times \Delta_{smth}^k)
                  for the subcomplex of forms that in addition are
