          %p
            Notice that the entries of this table lie on four diagonal lines. It turns out that each cocycle below and to the left of another cocycle arises from it by an super Lie alghebraic incarnation of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            %em
              %a{:href => "#DoubleDimensionalReduction"} Double dimensional reduction
          #TheWZWTermsForStringAndMembrane.num_remark
            %h6#remark_14 Remark
            %p
              Here “
              %strong>
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+WZW+term"} higher WZW term
              ” means the following:
            %p
              Regard
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi μ
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mover
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mi a
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo )
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_{F1} = \left(\overline{\psi} \wedge \Gamma_a \psi\right) \wedge e^a
              as a left
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+differential+form"} invariant differential form
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-Minkowski+spacetime"} super-Minkowski spacetime
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi B
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_{F1}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi dR
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mover
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mi a
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo )
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi a
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{dR} B_{F1} = \left(\overline{\psi} \wedge \Gamma_a \psi\right) \wedge e^a
                    \\,.
            %p
              (This
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_{F1}
              will
              = succeed ".)" do
                %em not be left-invariant
            %p
              Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superstring"} superstring
              is the function on the space of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Σ
                            %mn 2
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mtext worldsheet
                    %mo ⟶
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mrow
                              %mn 9
                              %mo ,
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi N
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mtext super-spacetime
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi \;\colon\; \underset{\text{worldsheet}}{\underbrace{\Sigma_2}}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    \\underset{\text{super-spacetime}}{\underbrace{\mathbb{R}^{9,1\vert \mathbf{N}}}}
            %p
              (morphisms of
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifolds"} supermanifolds
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∫
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi Σ
                                %mn 2
                          %msqrt
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi det
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mi i
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mi j
                              %msub
                                %mi e
                                %mi b
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi d
                          %msup
                            %mi σ
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ∧
                          %mi d
                          %msup
                            %mi σ
                            %mn 2
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mtext kinetic action
                    %mo +
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∫
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi Σ
                                %mn 2
                          %msup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mo *
                          %msub
                            %mi B
                            %mrow
                              %mi F
                              %mn 1
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mtext WZW term
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi
                    \\;\mapsto\;
                    \\underset{\text{kinetic action}}{
                    \\underbrace{
                    \\int_{\Sigma_2}
                    \\sqrt{
                    \-det(\partial_{\sigma^i} e^a(\phi) \partial_{\sigma_j} e_b(\phi))
                    }
                    \\,
                    d \sigma^1 \wedge d\sigma^2
                    }}
                    +
                    \\underset{\text{WZW term}}{
                    \\underbrace{
                    \\int_{\Sigma^2} \phi^\ast B_{F1}
                    }
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              The first term is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nambu-Goto+action"} Nambu-Goto action
              the second is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+term"} WZW term
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p
              Originally
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional#GreenSchwarz84"} Green-Schwarz 84
              introduced
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_{F1}
              to ensure an additional fermionic symmetry: “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kappa-symmetry"}> kappa-symmetry
              ”.
            %p
              Notice that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B_{F1}
              looks somewhat complicated and is not unique. That it is simply a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW-term"} WZW-term
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergroup"} supergroup
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 9
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi N
                    %mo =
                    %mi Iso
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 9
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi Spin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 9
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{9,1\vert \mathbf{N}}
                    \=
                    Iso(\mathbb{R}^{9,1\vert \mathbf{N}}) / Spin(9,1)
            %p
              was observed in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/source/Green-Schwarz+action+functional#HenneauxMezincescu85"} Henneaux-Mezincescu 85
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p
              Similarly, choose any differential form potential
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{M2}
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi dR
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mover
                        %mi ψ
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi Γ
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mi b
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo )
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi a
                    %mo ∧
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mi b
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_{dR} C_{M2} = \left(\overline{\psi} \wedge \Gamma_{a b} \psi\right) \wedge e^a \wedge e^b
                    \\,.
            %p
              (This
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mrow
                        %mi M
                        %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{M2}
              will
              = succeed ".)" do
                %em not be left-invariant
            %p
              Then the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz type action functional
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermembrane"} supermembrane
              is the function on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} fields
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Σ
                            %mn 3
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mtext worldvolume
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mn 10
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 32
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi \;\colon\; \underset{\text{worldvolume}}{\underbrace{\Sigma_3}} \longrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{10,1\vert \mathbf{32}}
            %p given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ↦
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∫
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi Σ
                                %mn 2
                          %msqrt
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi det
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mrow
                                  %msup
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mi i
                              %msup
                                %mi e
                                %mi a
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mrow
                                  %msub
                                    %mi σ
                                    %mi j
                              %msub
                                %mi e
                                %mi b
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi ϕ
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                          %mi d
                          %msup
                            %mi σ
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ∧
                          %mi d
                          %msup
                            %mi σ
                            %mn 2
                          %mo ∧
                          %mi d
                          %msup
                            %mi σ
                            %mn 3
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mtext kinetic action
                    %mo +
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∫
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi Σ
                                %mn 3
                          %msup
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mo *
                          %msub
                            %mi C
                            %mrow
                              %mi M
                              %mn 2
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mtext WZW term
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\phi
                    \\;\mapsto\;
                    \\underset{\text{kinetic action}}{
                    \\underbrace{
                    \\int_{\Sigma_2}
                    \\sqrt{
                    \-det(\partial_{\sigma^i} e^a(\phi)\partial_{\sigma_j} e_b(\phi))
                    }
                    \\,
                    d \sigma^1 \wedge d\sigma^2 \wedge d\sigma^3
                    }}
                    +
                    \\underset{\text{WZW term}}{
                    \\underbrace{
                    \\int_{\Sigma^3} \phi^\ast C_{M2}
                    }
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              On the right this is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+WZW+term"} higher WZW term
          %h3#ExtendedSuperMinkowskiSpacetime Extended super Minkowski spacetimes
          %p
            This way we may finally continue the progression of invariant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/central+extensions"} central extensions
            to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+central+extensions"} higher central extensions
          %p
            Recall from prop.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HomotopyFibersOfLInfinityCocycles"}
            that and how higher cocycles classify
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+central+extensions"} higher central extensions
