                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            The advantage of this perspective on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            from the point of view of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+field"} background flux fields
            is that powerful tools from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            theory apply.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            To first approximation background fluxes represent classes in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            (their
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charges"} charges
          %p
