                  \\longrightarrow
                  B^2 \mathbb{Z} \;\times\; B^3 \mathbb{Z} \;\times\; B^4 \mathbb{Z}  \;\times\; B^6 \mathbb{Z} \;\times\; B^7 \mathbb{Z}
                  \\,.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p We ask:
          %p
            %em Which mathematical operation could cause such a transmutation?
          %p
            We will now find such an operation and then use it to give an improved definition of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h3#DoubleDimensionalReductionViaFreeLooping Via free looping (no 0-brane effect)
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p Let’s first record formally what was going on in the above story.
          %p
            In the above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            of the naive M-fluxes on a trivial 11d circle bundle we used
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+product"} Cartesian product
                with the circle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functions"} functions
                out of the circle.
          %p Let’s have a closer look at these two operations:
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            It is a classical fact about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+spaces"} locally compact topological spaces
            (which includes all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            that one cares about in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physics"} physics
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+bijection"} natural bijection
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mtext continuous functions
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Σ
                            %mo ×
                            %mi F
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi X
                    %mo }
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munderover
                    %mo ↔
                    %mtext "forming adjuncts"
                    %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mtext continous functions
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Σ
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mi Maps
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo ,
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  \\text{continuous functions}
                  \\\
                  \\Sigma \times F \longrightarrow X
                  }
                  \\right\}
                  \\;\;
                  \\underoverset
                  {\text{"forming adjuncts"}}
                  {\simeq}
                  {\leftrightarrow}
                  \\;\;
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  \\text{continous functions}
                  \\\
                  \\Sigma \longrightarrow Maps(F,X)
                  }
                  \\right\}
          %p where
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \times X
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+space"} product topological space
                of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                with
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %p
                (the set of pairs of points euipped with the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topology"} product topology
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps(F,Y)
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+space"} mapping space
                from
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                to
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %p
                (the set of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functions"} continuous functions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \to X
                equipped with the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact-open+topology"} compact-open topology
          %p
            Except for the subtlety with the topology this bijection is just rewriting a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            of two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/variables"} variables
            as a function with values in a second function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\tilde f(a))(b) = f(a,b)
                  \\,.
          %p
            One says that the two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi cg
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munderover
                    %mo ⊥
                    %munder
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mrow
                        %mi Maps
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟵
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                        %mo ×
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi cg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Top_{cg}
                  \\;
                  \\underoverset
                  {\underset{Maps(F,-)}{\longrightarrow}}
                  {\overset{F \times (-)}{\longleftarrow}}
                  {\bot}
                  \\;
                  Top_{cg}
          %p
            form a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint pair
            or an
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            A remarkable amount of structure comes with every
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi id
                      %mi F
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \times X \overset{id}{\to} F \times X
                generally called the
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} unit of the adjunction
                %strong wrapping operation
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mi F
                      %mo ×
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      X \overset{}{\longrightarrow} Maps(F, F \times X)
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity"} identity
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo →
                        %mi id
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps(F,X) \overset{id}{\to} Maps(F,X)
                generally called the
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit+of+an+adjunction"} counit of the adjunction
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/evaluation+map"} evaluation map
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi ev
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      F \times Maps(F, X) \overset{ev}{\longrightarrow} X
              %p that evaluates a function on an argument
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            We will see now that the following general fact about
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
            serves to implement the above physics story of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/wrapped+branes"} wrapped branes
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            %strong Fact.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunct"} adjunct
            of a map of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi F
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G \;\colon\; F \times X \overset{}{\longrightarrow} A
          %p
            is the composite of its image under
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Maps(F,-)
            with the adjunction unit
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi η
                        %mi X
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi F
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mi Maps
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo ,
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tilde G
                  \\;\colon\;
                  X \overset{\eta_X}{\longrightarrow} Maps(F,F \times X)
                  \\overset{Maps(F,G)}{\longrightarrow}
                  Maps(F,A)
          %p
            Moreover, we will see that the following generall fact in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            accurately implements the idea of dimensional reduction of the brane dimensions:
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F = S^1
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mi X
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{L} X
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  Maps(S^1, X)
          %p
            is also called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+space"} free loop space
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          #FreeLoopSpacesOfDeloopedAbelianInfinityGroups.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_20 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              a general
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+space"} free loop space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi ad
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Maps(S^1, B G)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    G/_{ad}G
            %p
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weakly homotopy equivalent
              to the
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              by its
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+action"} adjoint action
            %p
              In the special case that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            %p
              then this becomes a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
              of following simple form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mi G
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mtext wrapped
                        %mrow
                          %mtext coefficient
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ×
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mi B
                          %mi G
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mtext plain
                        %mrow
                          %mtext coefficient
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Maps(S^1 , B G)
                    \\; \simeq \;
                    \\underset{\text{wrapped} \atop \text{coefficient}}{\underbrace{G}}
                    \\; \times \;
                    \\underset{\text{plain} \atop \text{coefficient}  }{\underbrace{ B G }}
                    \\,.
            %p
              %em This captures the required reduction on brane dimension!
            %p
              In particular if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = B^n \mathbb{Z}
              then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ×
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Maps(S^1, B^{n+1} \mathbb{Z}) \;\;  \simeq B^n \mathbb{Z} \;\times\; B^{n+1} \mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          #ReductionOfGFluxChargesOnTrivialCircleFibration.num_example
            %h6#example_14 Example
            %p
              Consider naive
              = succeed "-flux" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_7
              on an 11d spacetime that is a trivial circle bundle
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 11
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi X
                        %mn 10
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{11} = X_{10} \times S^1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 7
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 10
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mn 4
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mn 7
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ([G_4], [G_7])
                    \\;\colon\;
                    X_{10} \times S^1 \longrightarrow B^4 \mathbb{Z} \times B^7 \mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              this is identified with a map of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 6
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 7
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 4
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 7
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ˜
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 10
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Maps
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mn 4
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mn 7
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mn 3
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ×
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mn 4
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ×
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mn 6
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ×
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mn 7
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left([H_3], [F_4], [F_6], [H_7]\right)
                    \\,\coloneqq\,
                    \\widetilde{([G_4], [G_7])}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    X_{10}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Maps\left(
                    S^1,
                    \\; B^4 \mathbb{Z} \times B^7 \mathbb{Z}  \;
                    \\right)
                    \\;\;\simeq\;\;
                    B^3 \mathbb{Z}
                    \\;\times\;
                    B^4 \mathbb{Z}
                    \\;\times\;
                    B^6 \mathbb{Z}
                    \\;\times\;
                    B^7 \mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
            %p
              where on the right we have the transmuted
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeLoopSpacesOfDeloopedAbelianInfinityGroups"}
          %p This is exactly the result we were after.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            Better yet, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            yoga accurately reflects the physics story: For consider a
            = succeed "-brane" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trajectory"} trajectory
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi p
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi p
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 10
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\phi_p \;\colon\; \Sigma_p \longrightarrow X_{10}
          %p and coupled to these dimensionally reduced background fields
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi p
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi p
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 10
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 6
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 7
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 3
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ×
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 4
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ×
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 6
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ×
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 7
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≃
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 4
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ×
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 7
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma_p
                  \\overset{\phi_p}{\longrightarrow}
                  X_{10}
                  \\overset{([H_3], [F_4], [F_6], [H_7])}{\longrightarrow}
                  B^3 \mathbb{Z} \;\times\; B^4 \mathbb{Z} \;\times\; B^6 \mathbb{Z} \;\times\; B^7 \mathbb{Z}
                  \\;\;\;\simeq\;\;\;
                  Maps(S^1, B^4 \mathbb{Z} \,\times\, B^7 \mathbb{Z})
                  \\,.
          %p
            By
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            this is identified with a map of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi p
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ϕ
                        %mi p
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 10
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 11
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi G
                        %mn 7
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 4
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ×
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msup
                    %mi B
                    %mn 7
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Sigma_p \times S^1
                  \\overset{\phi_p \times S^1}{\longrightarrow}
                  X_{10} \times S^1 = X_{11}
                  \\overset{([G_4], [G_7])}{\longrightarrow}
                  B^4 \mathbb{Z} \;\times\; B^7 \mathbb{Z}
          %p and this is exactly the coupling we saw in the story of double dimensional reduction.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p So this works well as far as it goes, but so far it only applies to trivial circle fibrations and it does not see the D0-charge.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p We now disucss the improvement to the full formulation.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %h3#DoubleDimensionalReductionViaCyclification Via cyclification (with 0-brane effects)
          %p In general the M-theory circle bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↪
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 11
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 10
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  S^1 &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; X_{11}
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; X_{10}
                  }
          %p
            is only locally a product with of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 10
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{10}
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            For example the complement of the locus of a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-monopole"} KK-monopole
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundle"} principal U(1)-bundle
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
            equal to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
            carried by the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-monopole"} KK-monopole
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
            in type IIA).
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            Hence in general the above formulation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            via the pair of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S^1 \times (-) \;\;\dashv\;\; Maps(S^1, -)
          %p works only locally.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            But the problem to be solved is easily identified: Essentially by definition, in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            may all be identified with a fixed abstract
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            only
            = succeed "." do
              %em up to rigid rotation
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p Hence while in general the above wrapping-map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 10
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 11
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X_{10} \overset{}{\longrightarrow} Maps(S^1, X_{11})
          %p
            given by sending each point of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 10
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{10}
            to its fiber “wrapping around itself” does not exist, it does exist up to forgetting at which point in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
            we start the wrapping, hence the map that always exists lands in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+space"} quotient space
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 11
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mtext continuous functions
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi S
                                %mn 1
                              %mo ⟶
                              %msub
                                %mi X
                                %mn 11
                      %mo }
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mtext rigid loop rotations
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi S
                                %mn 1
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %mi t
                                  %mo ↦
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mi t
                                  %mo +
                                  %msub
                                    %mi t
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %msup
                                %mi S
                                %mn 1
                      %mo }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Maps(S^1, X_{11})/S^1
                  \\;=\;
                  \\frac{
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  \\text{continuous functions}
                  \\\
                  S^1 \longrightarrow X_{11}
                  }
                  \\right\}
                  }{
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  \\text{rigid loop rotations}
                  \\\
                  S^1 \overset{t \mapsto (t + t_0)}{\longrightarrow} S^1
                  }
                  \\right\}
                  }
          %p
            In general we take this to be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
            space.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            There is then the following generalization of proposition
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeLoopSpacesOfDeloopedAbelianInfinityGroups"}
            on transmutation of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
          #FreeLoopSpacesModS1OfDeloopedAbelianInfinityGroups.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_21 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            %p
              Then there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+homotopy+equivalence"} weak homotopy equivalence
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Maps
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %munder
                        %munder
                          %mi G
                          %mo ⏟
                        %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mi wrapped
                          %mrow
                            %mi coefficient
                      %mo ×
                      %munder
                        %munder
                          %mrow
                            %mi B
                            %mi G
                          %mo ⏟
                        %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mi plain
                          %mrow
                            %mi coefficient
                      %mo )
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ×
                            %mrow
                              %msup
                                %mi S
                                %mn 1
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mi twist
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mi E
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mtext D0-brane
                        %mrow
                          %mi coeff
                          %mo .
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Maps(S^1 , B G)/S^1
                    \\; \simeq \;
                    \\left(
                    \\underset{wrapped \atop coefficient}{\underbrace{G}}
                    \\times
                    \\underset{plain \atop coefficient}{\underbrace{B G}}
                    \\right)
                    \\underset{twist}{
                    \\underbrace{
                    \\times_{S^1}
                    }
                    }
                    \\underset{\text{D0-brane} \atop coeff.}{\underbrace{E S^1}}
                    \\,.
          %p
            Notice that a twisting appears. This is a general phenomenon. We will see
            %a{:href => "#KKReductionToIIA"} below
            that for the example of reduction of M-flux the twist that appears is that in the twisted de Rham cohomology
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 4
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ∧
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d F_4 = H_3 \wedge F_2
            which connects RR-fields
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_{2p}
            with the H-flux
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_3
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            Indeed this dimensional reduction is again an
            %em equivalent
            way of regarding the higher dimensional situation:
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          #CorrectReductionOnTopologicalSpaces.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_22 Proposition
            %p
              %strong (double dimensional reduction on topological flux fields)
            %p
              There is a pair of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} adjoint (∞,1)-functors
              really)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo {
                              %mi spaces
                              %mo }
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⊥
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %mi Maps
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msup
                                    %mi S
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                  %msup
                                    %mi S
                                    %mn 1
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟵
                                %mi hofib
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo {
                              %mtext spaces over
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mi B
                              %msup
                                %mi S
                                %mn 1
                              %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\left\{
                    spaces
                    \\right\}
                    \&amp;
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{Maps(S^1,-)/S^1}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{hofib}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    \&amp;
                    \\left\{
                    \\text{spaces over}\, B S^1
                    \\right\}
                    }
            %p
              (a proof in more generality is below after prop.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#GeneralReduction"}
              = succeed "):" do
                %a{:href => "#NSS12"} Nikolaus-Schreiber-Stevenson 12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
              (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-functors"} adjoint (∞,1)-functors
              really)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo {
                              %mi spaces
                              %mo }
                          %mtd
                            %munderover
                              %mo ⊥
                              %munder
                                %mo ⟶
                                %mrow
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                  %mi Maps
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msup
                                    %mi S
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo →
                                  %mi Maps
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %msup
                                    %mi S
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo ,
                                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                                  %msup
                                    %mi S
                                    %mn 1
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mover
                                %mo ⟵
                                %mtext total space
                          %mtd
                            %mrow
                              %mo {
                              %msup
                                %mi S
                                %mn 1
                              %mtext -principal
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mn ∞
                              %mtext -bundles
                              %mo }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\left\{
                    spaces
                    \\right\}
                    \&amp;
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{[Maps(S^1,-) \to Maps(S^1,-)/S^1]}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{\text{total space}}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    \&amp;
                    \\left\{
                    S^1\text{-principal}\;\infty\text{-bundles}
                    \\right\}
                    }
            %p Hence for
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mrow
                                %mi d
                                %mo +
                                %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi d
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^1 &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; X_{d+1}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; X_{d}
                    }
            %p
              an
              = succeed "-principal" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              some
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+equivalence"} natural equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mi Hom
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mrow
                              %mi d
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mtext original
                        %mrow
                          %mtext fluxes
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munderover
                      %mo ≃
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mtext reduction
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mtext oxidation
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mi B
                              %msup
                                %mi S
                                %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi d
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo ,
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ℒ
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                        %mrow
                          %mtext doubly
                        %mrow
                          %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mtext dimensionally  reduced
                            %mrow
                              %mtext fluxes
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{
                    \\text{original} \atop \text{fluxes}
                    }{
                    \\underbrace{
                    Hom(X_{d+1}\;,\; A)
                    }
                    }
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{\text{reduction}}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{\text{oxidation}}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\simeq}
                    \\;\;\;
                    \\underset{
                    \\text{doubly} \atop { \text{dimensionally  reduced} \atop \text{fluxes} }
                    }{
                    \\underbrace{
                    Hom_{/B S^1}( X_{d} \; ,\; (\mathcal{L} A)/S^1 )
                    }
                    }
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            Accordingly we have the following generalization of example
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReductionOfGFluxChargesOnTrivialCircleFibration"}
            to the case with possibly non-trivial circle-fibration and non-trivial D0-flux:
          #ReductionOfGFluxChargesOnTrivialCircleFibration.num_example
            %h6#example_15 Example
            %p
              Consider naive
              = succeed "-flux" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_4
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_7
              on an 11d
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
              that is an
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↪
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mn 11
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mn 10
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S^1 &amp;\hookrightarrow&amp; X_{11}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; X_{10}
                    }
            %p Its charges is represented by a map of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 4
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 7
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 11
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mn 4
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ×
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi B
                      %mn 7
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ([G_4], [G_7])
                    \\;\colon\;
                    X_{11} \longrightarrow B^4 \mathbb{Z} \;\times\; B^7 \mathbb{Z}
                    \\,.
            %p
              By
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
              this is identified with a map of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 3
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 4
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi F
                        %mn 6
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mn 7
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 4
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 7
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ˜
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mn 10
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Maps
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mn 4
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo ×
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mn 7
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi E
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mn 3
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ×
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mn 4
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ×
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mn 6
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ×
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msup
                        %mi B
                        %mn 7
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\left([F_2], [H_3], [F_4], [F_6], [H_7]\right)
                    \\,\coloneqq\,
                    \\widetilde{([G_4], [G_7])}
                    \\;\colon\;
                    X_{10}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    Maps\left(
                    S^1,
                    \\; B^4 \mathbb{Z} \times B^7 \mathbb{Z}  \;
                    \\right)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    E S^1
                    \\;\times_{S^1}\;
                    \\left(
                    B^3 \mathbb{Z}
                    \\;\times\;
                    B^4 \mathbb{Z}
                    \\;\times\;
                    B^6 \mathbb{Z}
                    \\;\times\;
                    B^7 \mathbb{Z}
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
              where on the right we transmuted the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              by prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FreeLoopSpacesModS1OfDeloopedAbelianInfinityGroups"}
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
            %p
              Hence the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D0-brane"} D0-brane
              charge appears! It is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+Chern+class"} first Chern class
              of the M-theory circle bundle.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            %strong Conclusion
          %p The double dimensional reduction of any flux field
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi G
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X_{d+1}
                  \\overset{G}{\longrightarrow}
                  A
          %p is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mi d
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mover
                              %mi G
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi Maps
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↙
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  X_{d}
                  \&amp;&amp; \overset{\tilde G}{\longrightarrow} &amp;&amp;
                  Maps(S^1, A)/S^1
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \searrow &amp;&amp; \swarrow
                  \\\
                  \&amp;&amp; B S^1
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p The operation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℒ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi Maps
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{L}(-)/S^1
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  Maps(S^1, -)/S^1
          %p
            may be called
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+loop+space"} cyclification
            because the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of this quotient of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+loop+space"} free loop space
            is
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+cohomology"} cyclic cohomology
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            Shadows of this construction appear prominently also at other places in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            notably in discussion of the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witten+genus"} Witten genus
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transchromatic+character"} transchromatic character
                map
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            In fact this formalization of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+dimensional+reduction"} double dimensional reduction
            works with loads of further data taken into account, such as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetimes"} spacetimes
            and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential cohomology
            of flux fields.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \,
          %p
            For the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            cognoscenti, here is the fully general statement:
          #GeneralReduction.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_23 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              be any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
              such as
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical homotopy theory on topological spaces
                  as above
              %li
                %p
                  or better: the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+formal+smooth+infinity-groupoid"} supergeometric homotopy types
            %p
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-group"} ∞-group
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              such as
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
                  as above
              %li
                %p
                  or better
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
                  such as the smooth
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi S
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^1 \simeq U(1)
            %p
              then there is a pair of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+%E2%88%9E-functors"} adjoint ∞-functors
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi G
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mi G
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi hofib
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{H}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{[G,-]/G}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{hofib}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    \\mathbf{H}_{/\mathbf{B}G}
                    \\,,
            %p where
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi G
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [G,-]
                  denotes the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
                  in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi G
                        %mo ,
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [G,-]/G
                  denotes the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+quotient"} homotopy quotient
                  by the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conjugation+action"} conjugation
            %p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              equipped with its canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-action"} ∞-action
              by left multiplication and the argument
            %p
              regarded as equipped with its trivial
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "-action." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [G,-]/G
              is the right
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/base+change"} base change
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+product"} dependent product
              along the canonical
              = succeed ".)" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo *
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ast \to \mathbf{B}G
            %p Hence for
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat X \to X
                  a
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi G
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficient"} coefficient
                  object, such as for some
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+cohomology"} differential
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            %p
              then there is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+equivalence"} natural equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
